                <pb facs="0248" n="146" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg146"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-06-08"><hi rendition="#italic">June 8,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Root acknowledges dispatch No. 284 and directs Mr. Rockhill to inform the
                    Chinese Government that if indemnity is paid for losses of others by reason of
                    the riots of December 18, 1905, this Government will demand indemnities for
                    losses of American citizens caused thereby.</p>
            </div>
